IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssaa-types`
IMPORT `ssaa-rules`

-- Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Overpayment case` HAS
    `the overpayment`                                   IS A MAYBE `Overpayment facts`
    `the conduct`                                       IS A MAYBE `Offence facts`
    `the penalty`                                       IS A MAYBE `Penalty facts`

DECLARE `Overpayment position` HAS
    `amount recoverable`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `offence`                                           IS A MAYBE `Benefit offence`
    `maximum sentence`                                  IS A MAYBE `Maximum sentence`
    `administrative penalty`                            IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `last day to withdraw agreement`                    IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 71, 111A, 112, 115A
@export default The position under the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (UK) after a benefit overpayment: the amount recoverable under s 71; which offence (if any) is committed under s 111A or s 112 and its maximum sentence; and the s 115A administrative penalty and the last day to withdraw agreement to it. Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS AN `Overpayment case`  @desc The overpayment facts, the conduct, and the penalty facts
GIVETH AN `Overpayment position`
`the overpayment position for` c MEANS
    `Overpayment position` WITH
        `amount recoverable`                            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the overpayment`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST o  THEN JUST (`the amount recoverable under s 71 for` o)
        `offence`                                       IS
            CONSIDER c's `the conduct`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the benefit offence for` f)
        `maximum sentence`                              IS
            CONSIDER c's `the conduct`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST f  THEN `the maximum sentence for` (`the benefit offence for` f)
        `administrative penalty`                        IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST p  THEN JUST (`the administrative penalty for` p)
        `last day to withdraw agreement`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `the penalty`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST p  THEN `the last day to withdraw agreement for` p
